+# Secretary’s Office request for Mineta’s September 11 telephone logs
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD01–PD04 and Mineta operational-record acquisition. Two Office of the Secretary of Transportation FOIA exports identify a 2007 request for logs of September 11 calls to or from the office of Secretary Norman Mineta. The 2008 release shows a **March 13, 2008 close date** for that request. The reply, disposition and underlying logs remain unlocated. [2008 release, physical p. 36](https://www.governmentattic.org/2docs/FOIA_Logs_DOT_2005-08.pdf#page=36) · [Official 2011 export, p. 13](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/fy2007foialog.pdf#page=13)
+
+## Compare the same request across exports
+
+| Source | Control | Request date | Logged date | Close date |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 2008 release, physical p. 36 / FY2007 screen p. 9 of 15 | **2007-144** | **04/16/2007** | **04/16/2007** | **03/13/2008** |
+| January 3, 2011 official FY2007 export, p. 13 of 25 | **2007-0144** | Column omitted | **04/16/2007** | Column omitted |
+
+The numeric suffix, logged date and subject support the row match. Preserve the literal controls. The older embedded text reads **Mlneta** while the rendered subject reads **Mineta**. The later export renders and extracts **Mineta**. The older date columns are visible on physical p. 28 and were matched to the row on p. 36. The 2008 cover's **FY 2008-161** is the file number for the release of the logs, separate from the 2007 request about telephone records. [Older cover, physical p. 2](https://www.governmentattic.org/2docs/FOIA_Logs_DOT_2005-08.pdf#page=2) · [Older column headers, p. 28](https://www.governmentattic.org/2docs/FOIA_Logs_DOT_2005-08.pdf#page=28) · [Source hashes and exact locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+The **Close Date** is an administrative field for the request. The reviewed row provides no disposition category or record inventory. A disclosure, referral, denial, withdrawal or other closure would require the final response and associated processing records. The telephone events themselves require the actual logs and a basis for identifying the line and its clock. The scope of this request is the Secretary’s office, with coverage of other locations and communications systems open.
+
+## Scope of the two exports
+
+The older FY2007 screen displays **Total 256 Record(s)**. A reproducible exact control-line count in the later export gives **254 unique IDs**, from **2007-0001** through **2007-0255**, with **2007-0132** absent from that count. Preserve the displayed total and the separately computed count. The two exports use different fields. The older rows were not enumerated into a complete control-by-control difference list, and the export queries and inclusion rules remain unacquired. [2008 FY2007 screen, physical p. 28](https://www.governmentattic.org/2docs/FOIA_Logs_DOT_2005-08.pdf#page=28) · [2011 export, adjacent controls at p. 12](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/fy2007foialog.pdf#page=12)
+
+The two PDFs contain **77 pages** in total. A text-layer screen for the FAA report, case and release identifiers and declared Commission, QFR and NORAD terms found no exact hits. The narrower telephone subject produced one matched page in each PDF. This screen covers two FOIA request exports, with OCR and coverage limits. It leaves the Secretary’s controlled correspondence, FAA's signed disposition and OIG recommendation histories as separate systems and open acquisition targets. The already held 1993 correspondence handbook matched byte for byte on re-fetch and was treated as a duplicate. [Declared patterns and results](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+**Next records.** Seek the original **2007-144 / 2007-0144** request and any routing or search memorandum, the response associated with the recorded March 13 close date, and any enclosure or withholding inventory. If the logs become available, check event time and time base, line or endpoint identifiers, incoming or outgoing status, and coverage before comparing them to reported calls. The corrected May FAA answer, delivery acknowledgment, signed administrative determination and recommendation outcomes remain open. [Prior FAA FOIA log study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/tree/main/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-fy2007-foia-log-original-route-2026-11-08)
+
+Verified two export hashes and **24 fixed text anchors**, visually checked the selected fields and retained the literal identifier forms and original scans. Public analysis omits requester names and the unrelated log rows.
